# Tagging - creating a version tag in a Git repository during the CI/CD pipeline to mark a specific release of the code.
   - A tag is like a label attached to a specific commit so you can easily identify versions of your project.

# Bumping - increasing or updating a version number of something in a project - package, dependency, or application.

# utils - Utilities - small, reusable helper functions, scripts, or tools that make common tasks easier and more consistent.

# fatal - serious error that stops a process or program from continuing

# nonce - number used once - mainly to ensure security, prevent replay attacks, and verify authenticity in various systems
# nitpick - to look for very small, often unimportant flaws or details
# backlog - Work that has accumulated and still needs to be completed
# ninja - A build execution tool, similar to make, but optimized for speed.

# Snapshot = Work-in-progress version - development version of an artifact that is not final or stable.
 
